From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 13:40:39 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] venus: fail an import the renderer cannot serve, not the
 context

An import that names a resource the context does not hold marks the
command stream fatal. The stream is sticky, so the ring stops advancing
its seqno, and the guest waiting on that seqno has nothing left to wait
for: it spins until its own timeout and aborts the whole device with a
ring fatal error. One buffer a client offered that the renderer cannot
serve therefore takes down every context on the guest, including the
ones that were working.

The command already has an answer for this. A resource whose descriptor
kind the renderer cannot import returns VK_ERROR_INVALID_EXTERNAL_HANDLE
from the same function and leaves the ring serving; only the branch for
a resource identifier the context never attached destroys it instead.
A client asking to import a buffer the renderer cannot take is an
ordinary runtime refusal, not a corrupt command stream: the command is
well formed, it was decoded whole, and Vulkan defines the result.

Answer both import commands with that result. A stream that carries the
reply itself, or the decoder's own stream, still fails the context,
because a resource identifier is a protocol term there and nothing can
be answered without it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/venus/vkr_device_memory.c | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/venus/vkr_device_memory.c b/src/venus/vkr_device_memory.c
index 918e9b4efb813b6773a407e7b579640b8cb3a2d6..770b47170b9facfc2f623c2579a113422585fe0e 100644
--- a/src/venus/vkr_device_memory.c
+++ b/src/venus/vkr_device_memory.c
@@ -279,7 +279,6 @@ vkr_dispatch_vkAllocateMemory(struct vn_dispatch_context *dispatch,
       if (!res) {
          vkr_log("failed to import resource: invalid res_id %u",
                  res_info->resourceId);
-         vkr_context_set_fatal(ctx);
          args->ret = VK_ERROR_INVALID_EXTERNAL_HANDLE;
          return;
       }
@@ -612,7 +611,7 @@ vkr_dispatch_vkGetMemoryResourcePropertiesMESA(
    struct vkr_resource *res = vkr_context_get_resource(ctx, args->resourceId);
    if (!res) {
       vkr_log("failed to query resource props: invalid res_id %u", args->resourceId);
-      vkr_context_set_fatal(ctx);
+      args->ret = VK_ERROR_INVALID_EXTERNAL_HANDLE;
       return;
    }
 
